      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "If $2=\\frac{3}{10}hk,$ then $k=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $10$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{3}{10}hk \\\\ 10\\cdot 2 & =10\\cdot \\frac{3}{10}hk \\\\ 20 & =3hk\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to isolate $k.$ To do this, we divide both sides of the equation by $3h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20 & =3hk \\\\ \\frac{20}{3h} & =\\frac{3hk}{3h} \\\\ \\frac{20}{3h} & =\\frac{\\cancel{3h}k}{\\cancel{3h}} \\\\ \\frac{20}{3h} & =k \\\\ k & =\\frac{20}{3h}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
